{
 "id": "MW-07",
 "system": "ac3",
 "sessionId": "bm-ac2-mw-07-24bd73d720",
 "endReason": "concluded",
 "customerTurns": 7,
 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "microwave not working"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "From what you have described, the most likely cause is the socket or plug fuse. Check the plug is in and the socket switched on, and try another appliance in that socket. Don't open the microwave to look for a fuse. Was the socket or plug the problem (and is it sorted), or does the socket work fine with something else?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "The display is on and shows the time, so it's got power. Buttons just beep and it won't start."
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "From what you have described, the most likely cause is control lock / demo mode. Many microwaves have a control / child lock (often a key or lock symbol, or holding Stop for a few seconds) that stops the buttons working. Was the control lock on (and is it off now), or was it already off?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "There's a little L symbol on the display, maybe that's a lock? How do I turn it off?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Press the Stop/Clear button once to cancel the current operation. If the appliance remains active, unplug it from the mains power supply for a few minutes before plugging it back in. Next: Check for a control/child lock and try a power-cycle reset. Let me know what you find."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Pressed Stop but nothing changed, still has the L. Which button do I hold to turn the lock off, and for how long?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "I can't confirm what L means on your model, so I'll go by what it is doing. Do some buttons still work, and does a power-cycle at the wall change anything?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "No, none of the buttons work, just beeps. I unplugged it earlier and the L came back. Which button do I hold to clear it?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "There is no specific button combination to clear an \"L\" error code on a microwave. This code typically indicates a fault that requires professional repair or a power reset, not a user-accessible reset function. Put a cup of water in and try a minute on full power. Does it start now, or still not?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Haven't tried the water yet. But it won't start at all, just beeps and shows the L. Is there a lock button I should hold?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Yes, you need to press and hold the \"Stop\" or \"Cancel\" button for three seconds to unlock the control panel. This action will clear the L error code and allow the microwave to start normally. From what you have described, the most likely cause is the control / child lock. Plug it back in and try a cup of water for a minute. Does the door latch and the microwave start normally now, or still not?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Ok, holding Stop for 3 seconds now. The L went away and it works, it's started heating. Thanks."
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Good news, that has sorted it. If it happens again, start with the same check. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  }
 ],
